+- id: exp7000-certified-blinded-pwa-kan
+  title: Certified blinded PWA-KAN constraint ranker
+  track: verification
+  priority: critical
+  agent_type: codex
+  model: gpt-5.6-sol
+  requires_gpu: false
+  max_turns: 50
+  estimated_wall_time_min: 180
+  per_unit_rows: true
+  prior_failures:
+    - experiment_id: exp6988-certified-pwa-kan-ranker
+      verdict: blocked_gate_check_failed
+      addressed_by: "Exp6988 was blocked by the mutation-provenance shortcut in Exp6987. Exp6997 and Exp6999 now remove that channel, prove sidecar invariance, and expose only a frozen numeric allowlist before Exp7000 fits any ranker."
+      retire_if_same_verdict: true
+  milestone: 2026.09.613
+  deliverable: results/experiment_7000_certified_blinded_pwa_kan.json
+  gated_on:
+    - upstream: exp6999-blinded-feature-cold-audit
+      artifact_field: blinded_feature_bank_ready_score
+      op: '=='
+      value: 1
+  prompt: |
+    CONTEXT:
+    V612 never trained its proposed PWA-KAN because mutation provenance alone
+    predicted the exact label. Exp6997 removes authority metadata from the
+    learner view. Exp6999 independently releases that view only after exact
+    sidecar-invariance and shortcut checks. This task tests a learned
+    non-oracle energy on that released table. Exact execution evaluates the
+    ranker but never supplies an input feature or ranking decision.
+
+    Work at {project_root}. The execution date is {date}.
+
+    EXISTING CODE TO READ FIRST:
+    - {project_root}/CLAUDE.md and {project_root}/CODEX.md
+    - {project_root}/research-program.md
+    - {project_root}/research-references.md V613 Planner Refresh
+    - {project_root}/results/experiment_6977_certified_pwa_kan_energy.json
+    - {project_root}/results/experiment_6988_certified_pwa_kan_ranker.json
+    - {project_root}/results/experiment_6997_authority_sidecar_rebuild.json
+    - {project_root}/results/experiment_6999_blinded_feature_cold_audit.json
+    - {project_root}/python/carnot/models
+    - {project_root}/scripts/experiments/experiment_6977_certified_pwa_kan_energy.py
+    - {project_root}/openspec/capabilities/constraint-verification/spec.md
+    - {project_root}/openspec/capabilities/continuous-learning/spec.md
+
+    TASK:
+    Train and freeze one compact PWA-KAN constraint ranker from the blinded
+    learner view. Compare it with constant, normalized-likelihood, grouped
+    logistic, and size-matched MLP controls. Certify its piecewise-affine
+    abstraction with a real MILP solver before opening prospective held-out
+    labels.
+
+    CONCRETE STEPS:
+    0. PRECONDITIONS: require blinded_feature_bank_ready_score=1, 138 complete
+       learner rows, immutable learner and sidecar hashes, source-disjoint
+       train, calibration, and held-out groups, a supported KAN runtime, and a
+       working MILP solver. On failure, write blocked_certified_blinded_pwa_kan
+       with gate_check_summary. Do not declare partial for missing upstream
+       data.
+    1. Add REQ-VERIFY-7000 and RED tests before implementation. Cover feature
+       allowlisting, grouped splits, label timing, control parity, calibration,
+       PWA conversion, solver identity, bound violations, irrelevant-field
+       attacks, frozen-held-out timing, and both bare readiness fields.
+    2. Load features only through the Exp6997 learner loader. Materialize and
+       hash tensors before a separate authority join supplies train labels and
+       split routing. Refuse any label, split, source, mutation, authority,
+       commitment, categorical model-identity, or row-order feature.
+    3. Fit a compact spline KAN on train source groups only. Use calibration
+       groups for knot count, regularization, stopping, and threshold choices.
+       Freeze weights, knots, feature scaling, and model hash before reading
+       the 12 held-out fixture pairs.
+    4. Fit constant, mean normalized likelihood, grouped logistic, and
+       size-matched MLP controls with identical train and calibration access.
+       Match seeds, candidate sets, and group splits. No control may inspect
+       the exact evaluator before selecting.
+    5. Convert the frozen KAN to an explicit piecewise-affine abstraction over
+       the observed feature domain. Preserve every segment, breakpoint,
+       coefficient, quantization choice, approximation residual, and model-to-
+       abstraction hash.
+    6. Use an installed MILP solver, not interval stubs, to recompute output
+       bounds, local Lipschitz bounds, irrelevant-field invariance, finite
+       values, and decision stability around every held-out row. Preserve
+       solver version, status, gap, timeout, and witness rows.
+    7. Open held-out labels only after the model, controls, PWA abstraction,
+       certificates, and evaluation script hashes are frozen. Report paired
+       ranking accuracy, AUROC, exact-selection yield, calibration, bootstrap
+       intervals, and strongest-control deltas by source group.
+    8. Set pwa_candidate_artifact_complete_score=1 when all model, control,
+       PWA, solver, and held-out rows are terminal and replayable. Set
+       pwa_model_ready_score=1 only when certificates pass, direct leakage is
+       zero, and the PWA-KAN has a positive paired held-out interval over the
+       strongest matched non-oracle control. A completed scientific null still
+       sets the artifact-complete field to one.
+    9. Run focused tests, Ruff, OpenSpec coverage, artifact validation,
+       adversarial verification, row-consistency lint, and root-clutter checks.
+    10. REQUIRED ARTIFACT FIELDS: field_principles with one scientific
+        principle per required field and both
+        pwa_candidate_artifact_complete_score and pwa_model_ready_score;
+        preconditions_checked; inference_substrate
+        (deterministic_blinded_pwa_kan_training_and_milp_no_llm); duration_s;
+        source_artifact_hashes; learner_view_hash; sidecar_hashes;
+        feature_allowlist; rows; per_candidate_rows; per_pair_results;
+        grouped_split_rows; tensor_materialization_rows; label_access_rows;
+        model_training_rows; calibration_rows; frozen_model_rows;
+        control_definition_rows; control_fit_rows; pwa_segment_rows;
+        pwa_breakpoint_rows; pwa_coefficient_rows; approximation_residual_rows;
+        milp_solver_receipt_rows; milp_bound_rows; lipschitz_bound_rows;
+        irrelevant_field_invariance_rows; decision_stability_rows;
+        freeze_before_heldout_rows; heldout_metric_rows; paired_delta_rows;
+        bootstrap_interval_rows; source_group_rows; source_disagreement_rows;
+        direct_leakage_count; exact_oracle_used_for_ranking (false);
+        pwa_candidate_artifact_complete_score; pwa_model_ready_score;
+        random_seed; reproducibility_checksum; gate_check_summary with failed
+        check, expected value, and observed value for any blocked verdict;
+        verifier_is_oracle (false); verdict_class
+        (positive | circular_positive | null | blocked | disqualified | partial);
+        honest_verdict with a terminal prefix consistent with verdict_class.
+
+    Run command: cd {project_root} && .venv/bin/python scripts/experiments/experiment_7000_certified_blinded_pwa_kan.py --date {date}
+    Do NOT push. Do NOT modify scripts/research_conductor.py.
